What:		/sys/devices/.../<panel>/timings
		/sys/devices/.../<panel>/timing
Date:		October 2026
Contact:	ArkOS4Clone
Description:

		panel-simple exposes the timings parsed from the panel's DT
		"display-timings" node through two sysfs attributes on the
		panel device. This is a vendor extension, compatible with the
		ArkOS 4.4 kernel's; it only exists when the panel node
		contains a "display-timings" node.

		What:		timings
		Type:		RO
		Description:	List of the available timings with their
				index, resolution, refresh rate and the
				currently active entry:

				count: 2
				0: 640x480@59Hz (current)
				1: 640x480@60Hz

		What:		timing
		Type:		RW
		Description:	Index of the currently active timing. On
				write, the CRTC driving the panel is switched
				to that timing in an atomic commit, and the
				fbdev emulation's mode is updated so the
				timing survives the console taking the display
				back. The active timing also carries the
				connector's preferred mode flag, so KMS clients
				started afterwards pick it up.

				Writing an index >= count returns -ERANGE.
				Writing while no CRTC is driving the panel
				returns -ENODEV.
